  "pattern": "stack",
  "hints": [
   "Keep a stack of indices, seeded with -1 as 'the last position before a valid run can start'.",
   "On '(' push i. On ')' pop; if the stack becomes empty, push i as the new barrier.",
   "Otherwise the current run length is i - stack[-1]."
  ],
  "func": "longest_valid",
  "prompt": "s contains only '(' and ')'. Return the length of the longest contiguous piece of s that is a balanced bracket string.\n\nSignature:\n    def longest_valid(s: str) -> int:\n\nExamples:\n    longest_valid('(()') -> 2\n    longest_valid(')()())') -> 4",
  "starter": "def longest_valid(s: str) -> int:\n    # Your code here\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "def longest_valid(s):\n    stack = [-1]\n    best = 0\n    for i, c in enumerate(s):\n        if c == \"(\":\n            stack.append(i)\n        else:\n            stack.pop()\n            if not stack:\n                stack.append(i)\n            else:\n                best = max(best, i - stack[-1])\n    return best\n",
