  "func": "count_smaller",
  "prompt": "Return a list where position i is how many values to the right of nums[i] are strictly smaller than it. Aim for O(n log n), for example with merge sort or a Fenwick tree.\n\nSignature:\n    def count_smaller(nums: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n\nExamples:\n    count_smaller([5, 2, 6, 1]) -> [2, 1, 1, 0]",
  "starter": "def count_smaller(nums: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    # Your code here\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "def count_smaller(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    counts = [0] * n\n    idx = list(range(n))\n    def sort(lo, hi):\n        if hi - lo <= 1:\n            return\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        sort(lo, mid)\n        sort(mid, hi)\n        merged = []\n        j = mid\n        for i in range(lo, mid):\n            while j < hi and nums[idx[j]] < nums[idx[i]]:\n                j += 1\n            counts[idx[i]] += j - mid\n        merged = sorted(idx[lo:hi], key=lambda k: nums[k])\n        idx[lo:hi] = merged\n    sort(0, n)\n    return counts\n",
